@page "/page-navigation"

<CatHead Title="In-page navigation">
    Moving around inside one long page: its contents, with the section in view marked, and a
    way back to the top.
</CatHead>

<CatExample TExample="Examples.PageNavigation.Contents" Title="On this page" Demo="ex-demo--block">
    <p>
        <strong>Live &mdash; scroll it, or follow a link.</strong> <code>.page-toc</code> is a
        <code>&lt;nav&gt;</code> of bare fragment links to the page&rsquo;s section headings, with one
        level of sub-sections in a nested <code>.page-toc-list</code>. Following one moves the reader
        and focus to its heading. With <code>data-spy</code> on the nav the script marks the link to
        the section in view <code>aria-current="location"</code>: the one whose heading has most
        recently reached the top of the scroller, the first before any has, and the last once the
        page is scrolled to its end.
    </p>
    <p>
        Beside the content, put it in the aside of a
        <a href="/grid"><code>.sedna-split--sticky</code></a> split, which keeps it in view while the
        page scrolls past. Stacked above the content on a narrow screen,
        <code>.page-toc-fold</code> lets the reader fold it away; a <code>&lt;p&gt;</code> title and the
        list alone are the same contents without the fold.
    </p>
</CatExample>

<CatExample TExample="Examples.PageNavigation.BackToTop" Title="Back to top" Demo="ex-demo--block">
    <p>
        <strong>Live &mdash; scroll it.</strong> <code>.back-to-top</code> is the last thing in the
        page, a link to <code>#top</code>: the scroller it is in goes back to its start and focus
        moves there, so the next Tab is the first control on the page. It sticks to the bottom
        corner, clear of the home indicator and the bottom bar, and comes in once the page has
        scrolled a screen down &mdash; <code>--back-to-top-after</code>, shortened here to fit the
        box. Where the engine has no scroll-driven animation it is always there.
    </p>
</CatExample>
